# basePath DesignNand
// NAND

::Intro
@trigger    OnDesignSetupComplete
$set temp:hintGiven = 0
{@PAL} NAND, or “Not AND” gates are the foundation of every computer. I have billions!\nOutput HI unless A and B are both HI.

::Hints
@trigger    OnSingleTestComplete
@when       result == "failure"
$if temp:hintGiven == 0
    {@PAL}  <color=yellow>Hint:</color> Use A and B to control Gates. Use constants to send signals to X.
    $set temp:hintGiven = 1
$elseif temp:hintGiven == 1
    {@PAL}  <color=yellow>Hint:</color> If both A and B are HI, send LO to X. You can use two gates on one transistor to detect this.
    $set temp:hintGiven = 2
$elseif temp:hintGiven == 2
    {@PAL}  <color=yellow>Hint:</color> If A is LO, allow LO to flow to X. If B is LO, allow LO to flow to X.
    $set temp:hintGiven = 3
$elseif temp:hintGiven == 3
    {@PAL}  <color=yellow>Hint:</color> Use separate Gates for A LO and B LO to prevent Unstable signals.
    $set temp:hintGiven = 0
$endif